[COMMENTS]
STATION,Flat V Crump profile weir. Runoff reduced by groundwater abstraction for PWS. GENERAL: Flat V weir Crump profile weir, 1:20 cross-slopes, 12.5m wide constructed in 1971. Pre-1971, station was natural river section with stable riffle control. Above 2m left bank overtopped, right bank is steep cliff. STATION HYDROMETRY: Some shoaling u/s. Multiple ratings applied through the period of record. FLOW RECORD: Ratings reviewed in 2022 and data reprocessed from 1981. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2023 (WINFAP Files v12). FLOW REGIME: Aquifer provides significant baseflow and moderates flood peaks. Runoff reduced by groundwater abstraction for PWS.
CATCHMENT,Headwaters drain Radnor Forest - underlain by Silurian bedrock. Impermeable formations are covered by extensive alluvial gravel deposits in the valleys. Predominantly grassland catchment supporting rough grazing, with some forestry.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged above QMED. Good fit to rating.
Pooling Suitability,Few high flow gaugings. Rating does not account for non-modular conditions or out of bank flow.
[END]
